  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "Express $5{cos}^{2}\u2061{16}^{\u2218}-5{sin}^{2}\u2061{16}^{\u2218}$ as a single trigonometric ratio.",
  "worked_solution": "Our expression can be factored as follows:\n\n$$\n5({cos}^{2}\u2061{16}^{\u2218}-{sin}^{2}\u2061{16}^{\u2218})\n$$\n\nNow, let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}\u2061x-{sin}^{2}\u2061x=\\operatorname{cos}\u20612x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x={16}^{\u2218}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{2}\u2061{16}^{\u2218}-{sin}^{2}\u2061{16}^{\u2218} & =\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(2\\cdot {16}^{\u2218})=\\operatorname{cos}\u2061{32}^{\u2218}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5({cos}^{2}\u2061{16}^{\u2218}-{sin}^{2}\u2061{16}^{\u2218}) & =5\\operatorname{cos}\u2061{32}^{\u2218}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
